  "type": "multipleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A block <math><mi>M</mi></math> hangs vertically at the bottom end of a uniform rope of constant mass per unit length. The top end of the rope is attached to a fixed rigid support at O. A transverse wave pulse (Pulse 1) of wavelength <math><msub><mrow><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math> is produced at point O on the rope. The pulse takes time <math><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub></math> to reach point A. If the wave pulse of wavelength <math><msub><mrow><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math> is produced at point A (Pulse 2) without disturbing the position of M it takes time <math><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub></math> to reach point O. Which of the following options is/are correct?<br ><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/trwmfmvwmrggubfecgvxcxsgnizlumszgeecyksacypozubxdg.jpeg\"/></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "NZab1",
      "text": "The velocity of any pulse along the rope is independent of its frequency and wavelength",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "24LyY",
      "text": "The velocities of two pulses are the same at the midpoint of rope",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "jkTc4",
      "text": "The wavelength of pulse 1 becomes longer when it reaches point A",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "UIgJT",
      "text": "The time <math><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>O</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/4_solu_phys_pa1.jpg\"/></p><p>(i)  Speed of wave is property of medium so time taken to cross the string will be equal</p><p>(ii)  Speeds are same but velocity is vector, has opposite directions</p><p>(iii)  Wavelength <math><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow></mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>></mo><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub></math></p><p>(iv)   Velocity of any pulse is <math><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi> </mi><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math> and it is property of medium.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
